  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Env Doctor for DSH",
      "text": "> First-run environment checks: Node, DSH_HOME, writability, profile files, sessions, and API-key\n> presence. Local-only; no network, no key value read."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "```bash\nnode bin/dsh-env-doctor.mjs --home ~/.dsh --profile web\nnode bin/dsh-env-doctor.mjs --json\n```\n\nIn DSH:\n\n```text\nUse env_doctor with profile=web.\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Checks",
      "text": "- Node major ≥ 20\n- DSH_HOME exists and is writable\n- `profiles/<name>/cordis.patch.yml` and `package.json`\n- sessions directory\n- `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` presence"
    },
    {
      "section": "Limits",
      "text": "- No provider auth probe, network, plugin execution, or repair.\n- Layout may differ across DSH versions.\n- Presence of a key is not proof that it is valid."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm test\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Provenance",
      "text": "A small independent environment check. License: MIT."
